        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>An electrochemical technique where the analyte of interest is first electroplated onto the working electrode before being removed or &apos;stripped&apos; by applying an oxidising potential. During removal the cell current is measured as a function of time and as a function of the potential between the indicator and reference electrodes. The potential is varied as a square wave superimposed on a linear sweep.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://doi.org/10.1039/b806470k</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


