        <owl:annotatedTarget>A method for determining structure by measuring the change in direction or energy of scattered neutrons and the time since the indicent pulse (&apos;time-of-flight&apos;) for each neutron. Neutrons are scattered by the atomic nuclei in the sample, and suffer a loss of kinetic energy during collisions.</owl:annotatedTarget>
