        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHMO_0000437"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A type of laser spectroscopy where a fixed-wavelength infrared  or ultraviolet laser is used to excite the sample which is placed in an electric field. By varying the strength of the applied electric field some vibrational–rotational transitions can be made to coincide with the laser wavelength and the absorption of the laser light is measured.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>Stark spectroscopy</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>laser Stark spectrometry</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
