        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHMO_0000733"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A type of NMR spectroscopy using pulsed-field gradients where the rate of decay of NMR signals in each component of a sample mixture is measured across a series of experiments. The rate of signal decay is proportional to the diffusion coefficient for each component. The diffusion coefficient for each peak is measured and this information is used to construct a 2D spectrum.</obo:IAO_0000115>
