        <owl:annotatedTarget>A method where the sample mixture is first separated by high-performance liquid chromatography before being ionised by forcing a solution (usually in an organic solvent) of it through a small heated capillary (at a flow rate of nL min1) into an electric field to produce a very fine mist of charged droplets. The ions are then characterised according to mass-to-charge ratio and relative abundance by two mass spectrometers in series.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0640-0422</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
