        <obo:IAO_0000115>Spectroscopy where the Raman scattering of monochromatic light by a sample is detected. Two lasers (&apos;pump&apos; and &apos;probe&apos;) are mixed and focused on the sample cell. When the frequency difference between the lasers corresponds to a Raman transition, an acoustic signal (a sound wave produced by an increase in pressure) is generated and detected by a sensitive microphone.</obo:IAO_0000115>
