        <obo:IAO_0000115>A type of laser spectroscopy where the sample is illuminated with a laser of frequency ω whilst a direct-current electric field is applied, allowing the production of the second harmonic (2ω). This technique is used to induce an asymmetry in an otherwise symmetric material as a probe of the molecular hyperpolarisability.</obo:IAO_0000115>
