        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHMO_0001391"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A synthesis technique involving the transfer of a nanosized pattern to a material using a micelle solution of a block copolymer. A glass or silicon substrate is dipped into the solution, retrieved, and the solvent is allowed to evaporate in air. A plasma treatment (O2, H2 or Ar) is performed to remove the polymer shell leaving a pattern.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:created_by>https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5985-7429</oboInOwl:created_by>
        <oboInOwl:creation_date>2009-09-21T11:12:19Z</oboInOwl:creation_date>
