        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A synthesis technique involving the transfer of a nanosized pattern to a material using a micelle solution of a block copolymer. A glass or silicon substrate is dipped into the solution, retrieved, and the solvent is allowed to evaporate in air. A plasma treatment (O2, H2 or Ar) is performed to remove the polymer shell leaving a pattern.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://doi.org/10.1088/0957-4484/14/10/314</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


