    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHMO_0002687 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHMO_0002687">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHMO_0000937"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A plot of absorbance or emission vs. wavelength/wavenumber/frequency obtained through a Fourier transform of the times series of the absorption or emission of a sample that has been excited by an infrared-frequency pulse. The infrared light is introduced into a prism at an angle exceeding the critical angle for internal reflection. This produces an evanescent wave at the reflecting surface (a surface which is transparent to infrared such as thallium bromide) on which the sample is supported. The distortion of the evanescent wave by the sample is measured.</obo:IAO_0000115>
