            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A planned process that includes spinning a sample very rapidly at the magic angle (54.74 deg with respect to the direction of the magnetic field) in order to average anisotropic interactions between nuclei, which are usually averaged by Brownian motion in liquid samples, to zero.</obo:IAO_0000115>
